panvk: VK_EXT_external_memory_host for the pages of IOSurfaces, on Darwin

Applied by tools/mk-panvk.sh only, after tools/mesa/*.patch and the panvk patches before it, to Mesa 25.0.7 (Mesa's own
licence, MIT, applies to the lines it adds). Written for Scion, after tools/mesa/turnip-darwin.patch's import for Turnip.

Why. Every texture over an IOSurface is, in the Metal frontend (userland/src/metalvk), a no-copy buffer over the surface's
pages. PanVK imported no host memory, so metal2vulkan made each one a buffer of its own memory and copied the caller's bytes
into it at every commit, compared 4 KiB at a time (tools/metal/m2v/0002). The window server on Metal (build 53) spent 116 of
399 display-thread samples there during home swipes, at 120 to 168% CPU against GLES's 25 to 38% (docs/metal.md, phase 4).

What. On Darwin, PanVK offers VK_EXT_external_memory_host for the pages of IOSurfaces only:
  - panvk_AllocateMemory: a host pointer the frontend told src/hakios-drm is a surface's mapping (hakios_drm_host_surface) is
    imported as the surface's buffer, which HakiosMali makes by its ID (kHakiosMaliSurface, what pan_kmod_bo_import already
    does with a surface ID on Darwin). Any other pointer is refused (VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE), since HakiosMali has no
    buffer of a process's other pages, and so is a surface whose pixels do not start at its first page or that is smaller
    than the import. metal2vulkan takes the refusal as before: it copies.
  - vkGetMemoryHostPointerPropertiesEXT: the one memory type for a surface's pages, none for others.
  - minImportedHostPointerAlignment 16 KiB, a page of Darwin's on arm64.
  - external buffer properties and linear 2D images: importable from host allocations, never exported.
  - vkMapMemory of imported memory is the caller's pointer, and is never unmapped here.
The memory stays coherent the way the frontend keeps it for Turnip: it cleans and invalidates the CPU's cache lines of the
surfaces a command buffer uses at its commit and at its completion (flushSurfaces), and HakiosMali flushes a surface it is
named in a submission.

